<title>LITHUANIA: RUSSIA REMAINS AS LITHUANIA'S MAIN TRADING PARTNER.</title>
<headline>RUSSIA REMAINS AS LITHUANIA'S MAIN TRADING PARTNER.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's statistics</p>
<p>department said on Tuesday that Russia remained the country's</p>
<p>main trading partner, accounting for 23 percent of the</p>
<p>country's exports and 26.2 percent of imports in the first</p>
<p>quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The statistics department presented the following table:</p>
<p>		   Export  Import	 Exports	Imports</p>
<p>		   1Q 97    1Q 97	1Q 97  1Q 96  1Q 97 1Q 96</p>
<p>	     in MLN LTL  in MLN LTL  in%    in%    in%    in%</p>
<p>TOTAL	    3,328.1  4,865.1    100    100    100    100</p>
<p>EU		 1,172.6  2.069.3    35.2   34.8   42.5   28.2</p>
<p>CEFTA		 54.8    103.7     1.6    2.0    2.1    2.8</p>
<p>CIS		1,490.0  1,530.6    44.8   44.4   31.5   38.3</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>-</p>
<p>Russia	    795.2   1,276.5    23.9   23.3   26.2   30.5</p>
<p>Germany	   410.3     806.1    12.3   14.2   16.6   13.8</p>
